-## 17. Fixed Navigation Alignment ✅
+## 18. Fixed CC Outstanding Not Updating After Settlement ✅
 
-**Issue:** Navigation buttons appeared centered due to `justify-content: center` CSS, especially noticeable when fewer buttons were visible in annual view.
+**Issue:** The "Previous Month CC Bill (Unpaid)" field was not updating its value after settlement. The auto-calculation logic was re-running on every render and overwriting the settled amount with the original value from the previous month.
 
-**Fix:** Changed navigation alignment from `center` to `flex-start` (left-aligned):
+**Root Cause:**
+- When `renderMonthlyBudget()` was called after settlement, it triggered `applyMonthlyAutoValues()`
+- This function cleared all auto-linked fields including `creditCardOutstanding`
+- Then the auto-calculation logic ran and recalculated `creditCardOutstanding` from the previous month
+- This overwrote the settled value
+- Additionally, the auto-calculation logic was checking if value exists, which caused it to skip recalculation when navigating to a month that had been previously opened (even if the previous month was just closed)
 
-### CSS Changes
-- Changed `.month-nav` `justify-content` from `center` to `flex-start`
-- Applied to both desktop and mobile responsive styles
-- Navigation now consistently left-aligned regardless of button count
+**Example of the problem:**
+```
+Previous Month CC: ₹38,000
+Settle ₹10,000 from savings
+Data updated: creditCardOutstanding = ₹28,000
+renderMonthlyBudget() called
+applyMonthlyAutoValues() clears creditCardOutstanding
+Auto-calculation resets it to ₹38,000 from previous month
+UI still shows ₹38,000 (wrong!)
+```
+
+**Fix:** Modified auto-calculation logic to:
+1. Skip clearing `creditCardOutstanding` value (preserve it across re-renders)
+2. Only auto-calculate if month is NOT closed AND NO settlement made
+3. This ensures:
+   - When month first opens after previous month close: auto-calculate ✅
+   - When user settles: preserve settled value ✅
+   - When navigating away and back: preserve settled value ✅
+   - When month is closed: preserve closed value ✅
+
+### Clearing Logic
+```javascript
+// Skip clearing creditCardOutstanding - it's managed by settlement
+if (fieldId === "creditCardOutstanding") return;
+```
+
+### Auto-Calculation Logic
+```javascript
+// Only auto-calculate if month is not closed AND no settlement made
+// (settlements should be preserved, closed months preserve their values)
+const isMonthClosed = Boolean(monthData._monthClosed);
+const hasSettlement = monthData._ccSettlementAmount && monthData._ccSettlementAmount > 0;
+
+if (!isMonthClosed && !hasSettlement) {
+    // Calculate from previous month
+}
+```
+
+### Re-Calculation Logic
+```javascript
+// Skip creditCardOutstanding in buildMonthlyAutoValues
+if (fieldId === "creditCardOutstanding") return;
+```
 
-### Result
-- Navigation buttons stay on the left in both monthly and annual views
-- Consistent layout regardless of which buttons are hidden/shown
-- Better visual consistency
+**Impact:**
+- Settlement now immediately updates the UI
+- Value persists across re-renders
+- Auto-calculation runs when month first opens (not closed, no settlement)
+- Settlements are properly preserved during the month
+- Closed months preserve their values
+- Previous month close properly carries forward to next month
 
 **Files Modified:**
-- `assets/css/styles.css` (line 641 - desktop month-nav)
-- `assets/css/styles.css` (line 2876 - mobile month-nav)
+- `assets/js/app.js` (lines 1449-1451 - skip clearing creditCardOutstanding)
+- `assets/js/app.js` (lines 1460-1461 - skip re-adding creditCardOutstanding)
+- `assets/js/app.js` (lines 1468-1500 - conditional auto-calculation logic based on month closed and settlement status)
+- `assets/js/app.js` (lines 4177-4178 - updated tooltips for accuracy)
+
